## Instruction
Change the order in which the watchlist displays movies: every movie the user has NOT watched yet must appear before every movie that HAS been watched. The `movies` signal must produce the store's items sorted so that each item with `watched === false` comes before each item with `watched === true`, while items keep their current relative order within the unwatched group and within the watched group (a stable sort of the store's item order). Implement this inside the watchlist unit by deriving `movies` from the store reactively (e.g. `movies = computed(() => ...)` sorting `store.items()`), and make sure watchlist.html renders the list from `movies()` so the DOM order matches the signal. The ordering must update reactively when a movie's watched status changes via `toggleWatched` (component or store), and when items are added or removed. All other behaviour (remove, onRowClick, watchedCount, progress, announcement) and every existing exported signature stay unchanged; do not modify WatchlistStore or any other unit. You may add new tests for the ordering in your spec file, but do not change or remove existing tests; if an existing test asserts the old (unsorted) display order, report the conflict rather than editing it.

